{"abstract":"Perceived physical exertion is increased when exercise is performed on metformin treatment, but the clinical relevance of this is unknown. In this post hoc analysis of a randomized, controlled trial, we investigated whether metformin treatment was associated with lower levels of free-living physical activity.   Ninety individuals with overweight/obesity (BMI>25 m2/kg) and HbA1c-defined prediabetes (39-47 mmol/mol) were randomized to treatment with dapagliflozin (SGLT2-inhibitor; 10 mg once daily, n=30), metformin (850 mg twice daily, n=30) or no treatment (control, n=30) for 13 weeks in a parallel-group, open-label trial. Before (baseline), during (6 weeks) and immediately after (13 weeks) cessation of treatment, a 6-day assessment of physical activity and sedentary behaviour was performed using accelerometer-based physical activity monitors. Intention-to-treat analyses revealed no within-group changes or differences in change between the groups for any measures of physical activity or sedentary behaviour at neither 6 nor 13 weeks. Short-term metformin treatment does not reduce free-living physical activity level in individuals with overweight/obesity and HbA1c-defined prediabetes.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Karstoft, Kristian","Ried-larsen, Mathias","Bruhn, Lea","Pilmark, Nanna Skytt","Hansen, Katrine Bagge","Persson, Frederik","Jørgensen, Marit Eika","Blond, Martin Bæk","Færch, Kristine"],"cuid":["S02-099.92-716506"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Nordic"],"corresponding_author":["Karstoft, Kristian"],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Steno Diabetes Center Greenland"],"keyword":["Exercise","Metformin","Physical activity","Rate of perceived exertion","Sedentary behaviour"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of metformin treatment on volumes of free living physical activity and sedentary behaviour a post hoc analysis of the pre d trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375203581/manuscript_final_3_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Novo Nordisk Foundation, AstraZeneca AB, the Danish Innovation Foundation, and University of Copenhagen."],"id":"S02-099.92-716506","identifier":[{"id":"85180249149","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38053246","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c3dda65b-8361-403f-aee6-5976981353cf","sdu-2aa25c15-4b30-4e67-ab57-72a2c9452cfb"],"keyword":["Metformin","exercise","physical activity","rate of perceived exertion","sedentary behaviour"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2702D3872DCF7F43A81D229FCC0ED685"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375203581/manuscript_final_3_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Pharmacology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3"